statement:
Let P ∈ ℕ and let μ be a measure on ℝ^P (Borel σ-algebra). Let M, W ⊆ ℝ^P with W open and M μ-null-measurable, let θ, g : ℝ^P → ℝ, and let C ∈ ℝ. Assume:
(i) θ(x) > 0 for every x ∈ M;
(ii) θ is μ-integrable on M ∩ W;
(iii) g is a.e.-strongly measurable for μ⌞M = μ.restrict M;
(iv) |g(x)| ≤ C for μ⌞M-a.e. x;
(v) ∫_M θ(x)·(φ(x)·g(x)) dμ(x) = 0 for every C^∞ function φ : ℝ^P → ℝ with compact support and tsupport φ ⊆ W.
Then for μ⌞M-a.e. x, x ∈ W implies g(x) = 0.
